# promise: #752
# An extension's toolbar button opens Chrome's own popup even when descriptors 3 and 4 were open before
# Chromium started. Chrome's --remote-debugging-pipe (the trusted client Extensions.triggerAction needs) only
# reads fd 3 and writes fd 4, and Cra gave the pipe up when either was in use: on a Mac where macOS's own
# HIToolbox.rsrc and Localized.rsrc landed there first, every click opened the popup page in Cra's fallback
# window instead, Bitwarden 48 pt wide. Cra now holds 3 and 4 from the first line of
# main (taking over ones a launcher left open) and lets go of them just before Chromium starts.
# Here the launcher leaks both (hold-fds). The popup must be Chrome's, in Cra's popup frame, and see the site as
# its window's active tab; the fallback page window doesn't count.
hold-fds
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true}
extension ${FIXTURES}/PopupContextExtension
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=site
wait 2
cra://debug?extensionAction=${POPUP_CONTEXT_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=popup-context-current-site-last-site HTTP
cra://debug?extensionPopup=held
expect-log extension popup held: shown
reject-log extension action [a-z]+ failed
expect-log devtools pipe: descriptors 3 and 4 free for Chromium
reject-log fault:
